opus-mt-en-ROMANCE (ONNX, int8) - local translation model used by RfLauncher
===========================================================================

This folder redistributes, WITHOUT MODIFICATION, the following files of the
Hugging Face repository "Xenova/opus-mt-en-ROMANCE", revision
9d2ba69ac80c8e8453c3d9a1e2323a0e7b8ca3cd:

  onnx/encoder_model_quantized.onnx
  onnx/decoder_model_merged_quantized.onnx
  source.spm, target.spm, vocab.json,
  config.json, generation_config.json, tokenizer_config.json

Original model: "Helsinki-NLP/opus-mt-en-ROMANCE" (OPUS-MT), by the Language
Technology Research Group at the University of Helsinki (Helsinki-NLP).
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE in this folder).

ONNX conversion and int8 quantization: Xenova (Joshua Lochner), distributed
under the same Apache License, Version 2.0.

Reference: Jorg Tiedemann and Santhosh Thottingal. 2020. "OPUS-MT - Building
open translation services for the World". Proceedings of the 22nd Annual
Conference of the European Association for Machine Translation (EAMT).

The translation engine is ONNX Runtime (Microsoft Corporation), MIT License,
bundled inside RfLauncher.exe (package Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntime 1.22.1). The
tokenizer is Microsoft.ML.Tokenizers (.NET Foundation), MIT License.

Credit shown in the launcher (Notas tab):
  "Tradução local: OPUS-MT (Universidade de Helsinque), Apache 2.0; ONNX por
   Xenova; ONNX Runtime (Microsoft, MIT)."
